  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1233 PM CST Mon Nov 9 2026\n\nOverall quiet weather is expected through late week. Longwave upper \ntroughing will dominate the eastern CONUS and will keep upper flow \nout of the north to northwest over the FA. This will help to keep \nafternoon highs in the 60s and 70s each afternoon. Despite a weak \ncold front by mid week, a freeze is not expected across the FA \nthrough the next week. Our next possible storm system will come late \nFriday into early Saturday, through there is much uncertainty with \nwhether we will see rainfall with this system or if we will be \ndryslotted. The GFS still keeps us on the dryer side while the ECMWF \nis more generous with rainfall. Given the pattern will be a neutral \ntilt open wave trough, the drier forecast is currently favored.",
